  "title": "Shift Your Focus When Recurring Thoughts Distort Your Perception",
  "description": "Shift your focus when recurring thoughts distort your perception. Here’s how: - Notice the pattern: Ask, “Am I only paying attention to things that match my current thoughts or worries?” - Refocus intentionally: Consciously look for neutral or positive details you might be missing. - Write it down: Track recurring thoughts and their triggers to understand how they shape your attention. Example: If you’re focused on a mistake, you might miss the positive feedback from others.",
